  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 5^{x}\\). If \\(f(a) + f(a + 1) = 90\\), what is the value of \\(f(a)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "15"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(f(a + 1) = 5^{a + 1} = 5 \\cdot 5^{a} = 5 f(a)\\).",
    "So \\(f(a) + 5f(a) = 6f(a) = 90\\), and \\(f(a) = 15\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "a = symbols('a', real=True)\nsol = solve(Eq(5**a + 5**(a + 1), 90), a)\nassert len(sol) == 1 and simplify(5**sol[0]) == 15\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == 15",
